  "notes": [
    "Column \"amount\" is the detail column and \"total\" the net column; column headings are not printed.",
    "The figures are very large for a single first quarter (e.g. Share from Internal Revenue Collections 1,440,708,204.00, total cash inflow 3,959,730,114.35, larger than the full-year 2022 statement), and Cash at Beginning (129,751,191.41) is far below other years' balances. Several figures are identical to the 2023 column of the 2024 annual statement (2024-annual-cash-flows): Share from Internal Revenue Collections 1,440,708,204.00, Interest Expense 13,146.11, Purchase of Intangible Assets 2,671,798.50 and Payment of Loan Amortization 691,393.35, while others are close but different (e.g. Collection from taxpayers 1,512,647,474.99 vs 1,514,911,478.50). The page may therefore be a full-year 2023 statement labelled Quarter 1, 2024; the printed period is kept and figures are transcribed as printed.",
    "Whether the figures are for the quarter or year-to-date is not stated; cumulative left null."
